# Build-time (Vite) variables for production builds, including Workers Builds.
#
# This file is committed ON PURPOSE and must hold PUBLIC values only. A Turnstile
# site key is public by design (it ships inside the JS bundle). The matching
# secret (TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY) lives in the Worker: `wrangler secret put`.
#
# Why not `vars` in wrangler.jsonc? Those are Worker *runtime* bindings; Vite
# only inlines VITE_* from the build environment, so the SPA never saw the key
# and the widget silently disappeared (server then rejected the empty token).
VITE_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=0x4AAAAAAFu473J7AXeNkvOy
